  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Clayman feels like the strongest next choice because my listening to Colony, Reroute to Remain, and Soundtrack to Your Escape gives me a clear reason to explore more In Flames.",
    "The End of Heartache matches the heavy riffs and melody I want together, while The War Within connects with the thrash intensity I enjoyed in Advance And Vanquish."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "In Love & Death feels less suited to this session because I want heavier, riff-driven music more than an emotional rock direction.",
    "I cannot confidently identify BLEEDING, THE UNCENSORED, so I have less reason to choose it over releases with recognizable connections to my listening."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in rock does not mean every adjacent emotional or aggressive release fits what I want right now.",
    "Connections to Ten Thousand Fists or Tool make albums worth considering, but aggression or rhythmic complexity alone does not make them my first choice today."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated In Flames listening matters more to today's choice than a broad resemblance to heavy music.",
    "I can find City of Evil, Believe, Faceless, and L.D. 50 appealing without choosing them now; today I mostly want melody paired with heavy riffs, with room for a clear thrash connection."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my interest in heavy music, but my strongest choices depend on specific listening connections and the balance of riffs and melody I want today."
